<PageTitle>Field guide · Cryptid Companion</PageTitle>
<p class="eyebrow">THE FIELD GUIDE</p><h1>Your board. Your deductions.</h1>
<section class="panel narrow prose">
<h2>What the companion does</h2><p>The absent clue-holders answer your questions. They do not take turns, choose questions or searches, or suggest moves. Keep your real board, structures, and pieces on the table.</p>
<h2>Setup</h2><p>Build the shown layout with the six physical tiles. Match the terrain and animal outlines to the reference. Choose 3–5 clue-holders including yourself and your color. The setup card fixes every book’s clue; their intersection is exactly one space.</p>
<h2>Cubes mean no. Discs mean yes.</h2><p>Place two opening cubes for each simulated clue-holder at the listed coordinates. Choose and record two of your own cubes on spaces that fail your clue. Several players may place cubes on the same space; one player never places two pieces on one space.</p>
<h2>Questions</h2><p>Choose a simulated clue-holder and a space without any cubes. They place a disc if their clue allows that space, or a cube if it does not. If the answer is a cube, you must place an additional cube on a space that fails your own clue before another action.</p>
<h2>Searches</h2><p>You may search only a space that satisfies your own clue and has no cubes. Place your disc there. The other clue-holders respond in clockwise book order starting after you. Existing discs count as yes. Stop at the first no: that clue-holder places a cube, and later clue-holders reveal nothing. Every participant who placed a disc as part of this search must place a cube elsewhere; the companion lists the simulated placements and asks you to record yours. If everyone agrees, you found the habitat.</p>
<h2>Distance</h2><p>“Within N spaces” includes distance zero: a space containing the feature is within range. Animal territory belongs to its printed terrain as well. There are no wraparound edges.</p>
<h2>Reading the reference board</h2><p>Bear territory has a solid black inset hexagon; cougar territory has a dashed red one. Discs are larger than cubes, and pieces stay clear of coordinate labels. Hover or focus any legend item to highlight matching public spaces, or tap to pin it. Player legend items highlight only their recorded pieces. Settings lets you show or hide pieces and coordinate labels.</p>
<h2>Saved games & offline play</h2><p>Assignments, pieces, and the journal save on this browser after each action. Reloading or changing pages preserves them. Install the app or load a published version once while online to cache it for offline use. Browser storage can be cleared by your browser; private browsing may not retain it. Completed expeditions move to Past games at camp, with a read-only Review that leaves any current expedition untouched. Reviews retain their original board content. An update with changed content may require a new active game.</p>
<h2>Content</h2><p>The included board is the user-provided reference layout, not an asserted printed card number. The normal rule catalog contains 23 clue types. Your clue is assigned by the selected card. Additional layouts, structures, books, and fixed clue assignments are YAML content, and can be imported from camp. This is an independent companion, not an Osprey Games product.</p>
